# deploy/Caddyfile.safeer.prod — Safeer's site blocks for the edge Caddy,
# PRODUCTION. Replaces Caddyfile.safeer.staging at cutover, once the apex
# and www DNS records point at the VPS (docs/backend/DEPLOYMENT-VPS.md);
# never install both.
#
# Matches SITE_URL=https://safeer-sa.org in /srv/safeer/.env.
#
# - safeer-web is the web container's alias on the edge network
#   (deploy/docker-compose.yml); Caddy must be attached to that network.
# - No trusted_proxies: Caddy then treats every client as untrusted and
#   REPLACES any X-Forwarded-For it sends with the real client address. The
#   web server trusts exactly one hop (TRUST_PROXY=1), and so does the API
#   behind it, so ip_hash and every per-IP rate limit see the real visitor.
#   Adding trusted_proxies here would let a client choose its own IP.
# - No caching: every HTML response carries its own CSP nonce and
#   per-visitor state; caching is left to the app's own Cache-Control.
# - No encode: the web server already compresses its responses.
# - No request_body limit: Caddy has none by default, which covers the API's
#   10 MB document uploads.

safeer-sa.org {
	reverse_proxy safeer-web:4000
}

# One canonical host: www redirects to the apex, path and query kept.
www.safeer-sa.org {
	redir https://safeer-sa.org{uri} permanent
}
